The equation is the definition of an ellipse with foci at \((3,-4)\) and \((-5,8)\).  
The distance between the foci is

\[
\sqrt{(-5-3)^2+(8+4)^2}
=\sqrt{64+144}
=\sqrt{208}
=4\sqrt{13}.
\]

The answer is \(4\sqrt{13}\).

